{"id":28763,"slug":"the-american-friend","title":"The American Friend","year":1977,"country":"Germany","duration":126,"spine":793,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28763-the-american-friend","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/bfc170fd79de2f1298ae0115534a9594/YIHd0ub4uOeANf4KvdgkkwZFqg0p6D_large.jpg","description":"Wim Wenders pays loving homage to rough-and-tumble Hollywood film noir with The American Friend, a loose adaptation of Patricia Highsmith’s novel Ripley’s Game. Dennis Hopper oozes quirky menace as an amoral American art dealer who entangles a terminally ill German everyman, played by Bruno Ganz, in a seedy criminal underworld as revenge for a personal slight—but when the two become embroiled in an ever-deepening murder plot, they form an unlikely bond. Filmed on location in Hamburg and Paris, with some scenes shot in grimy, late-seventies New York City, Wenders’s international breakout is a stripped-down crime story that mixes West German and American film flavors, and it features cameos by filmmakers Jean Eustache, Samuel Fuller, and Nicholas Ray.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Wim Wenders","slug":"wim-wenders"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Dennis Hopper","role":"Tom Ripley","slug":"dennis-hopper"},{"actor":"Bruno Ganz","role":"Jonathan Zimmermann","slug":"bruno-ganz"},{"actor":"Gérard Blain","role":"Raoul Minot","slug":"gerard-blain"},{"actor":"Nicholas Ray","role":"Pogash/Derwatt","slug":"nicholas-ray"},{"actor":"Samuel Fuller","role":"The American","slug":"samuel-fuller"},{"actor":"Daniel Schmid","role":"Igraham","slug":"daniel-schmid"},{"actor":"Jean Eustache","role":"Friendly man","slug":"jean-eustache"},{"actor":"Lisa Kreuzer","role":"Marianne Zimmermann","slug":"lisa-kreuzer"},{"actor":"Peter Lilienthal","role":"Marcangelo","slug":"peter-lilienthal"},{"actor":"Sandy Whitelaw","role":"Doctor","slug":"sandy-whitelaw"},{"actor":"Lou Cassel","role":"Rodolphe","slug":"lou-cassel"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","pers